# Evening Adhkar
@id evening-adhkar
@version 1
@author santarl
@desc The evening remembrance of the Sunnah, for the end of the day.
@desc Ordered from the most to the least authentic: Quran and Sahih first, then reports with weaker or disputed chains. Swipe up or down for the meaning, the transliteration, then the grading, reward and source of each slide.
@desc Arabic follows Hisn al-Muslim; Quranic text is the Tanzil Uthmani text (tanzil.net), unmodified. Translation and transliteration are original.

---1
# Ayat al-Kursi
ٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ ٱلْحَىُّ ٱلْقَيُّومُ | Allah: there is no god but Him, the Ever-Living, the Self-Sustaining. | Allahu la ilaha illa huwal-hayyul-qayyum, | Status: Quran (2:255). Its timing and any reward narrations were not verified for this profile.
لَا تَأْخُذُهُۥ سِنَةٌ وَلَا نَوْمٌ | Neither drowsiness nor sleep overtakes Him. | la ta'khudhuhu sinatun wa la nawm,
لَّهُۥ مَا فِى ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَمَا فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ | To Him belongs whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth. | lahu ma fis-samawati wa ma fil-ard,
مَن ذَا ٱلَّذِى يَشْفَعُ عِندَهُۥٓ إِلَّا بِإِذْنِهِۦ | Who is there that can intercede with Him except by His permission? | man dhal-ladhi yashfa'u indahu illa bi'idhnih,
يَعْلَمُ مَا بَيْنَ أَيْدِيهِمْ وَمَا خَلْفَهُمْ | He knows what is before them and what is behind them, | ya'lamu ma bayna aydihim wa ma khalfahum,
وَلَا يُحِيطُونَ بِشَىْءٍ مِّنْ عِلْمِهِۦٓ إِلَّا بِمَا شَآءَ | and they encompass nothing of His knowledge except what He wills. | wa la yuhituna bishay'in min ilmihi illa bima sha',
وَسِعَ كُرْسِيُّهُ ٱلسَّمَٰوَٰتِ وَٱلْأَرْضَ | His Throne extends over the heavens and the earth, | wasi'a kursiyyuhus-samawati wal-ard,
وَلَا يَـُٔودُهُۥ حِفْظُهُمَا | and guarding them does not weigh on Him. | wa la ya'uduhu hifzuhuma,
وَهُوَ ٱلْعَلِىُّ ٱلْعَظِيمُ | He is the Most High, the Most Great. | wa huwal-aliyyul-azim.
---1
# Sayyid al-Istighfar
أَللَّهُمَّ أَنْتَ رَبِّى لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنْتَ خَلَقْتَنِى وَأَنَا عَبْدُكَ | O Allah, You are my Lord; there is no god but You. You created me, and I am Your servant, | Allahumma anta rabbi la ilaha illa anta, khalaqtani wa ana abduka, | Status: Sahih (Sahih al-Bukhari 6306, Shaddad ibn Aws). Reward: whoever says it by day with firm belief and dies that day before evening is among the people of Paradise; the same for one who says it at night and dies before morning.
وَأَنَا عَلَىٰ عَهْدِكَ وَوَعْدِكَ مَا ٱسْتَطَعْتُ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا صَنَعْتُ | and I hold to Your covenant and Your promise as far as I am able. I seek refuge in You from the evil of what I have done. | wa ana ala ahdika wa wa'dika mastata'tu, a'udhu bika min sharri ma sana'tu,
أَبُوءُ لَكَ بِنِعْمَتِكَ عَلَىَّ وَأَبُوءُ بِذَنْبِى | I acknowledge Your favour upon me, and I acknowledge my sin; | abu'u laka bini'matika alayya, wa abu'u bidhanbi,
فَٱغْفِرْ لِى فَإِنَّهُ لَا يَغْفِرُ ٱلذُّنُوبَ إِلَّآ أَنْتَ | so forgive me, for none forgives sins except You. | faghfir li fa'innahu la yaghfirudh-dhunuba illa anta.
---1
# Evening: dominion is Allah’s
أَمْسَيْنَا وَأَمْسَى ٱلْمُلْكُ لِلَّهِ وَٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ، لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ، لَهُ ٱلْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ ٱلْحَمْدُ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ، رَبِّ أَسْأَلُكَ خَيْرَ مَا فِى هَٰذِهِ ٱللَّيْلَةِ وَخَيْرَ مَا بَعْدَهَا، وَأَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا فِى هَٰذِهِ ٱللَّيْلَةِ وَشَرِّ مَا بَعْدَهَا، رَبِّ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنَ ٱلْكَسَلِ وَسُوءِ ٱلْكِبَرِ، رَبِّ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ عَذَابٍ فِى ٱلنَّارِ وَعَذَابٍ فِى ٱلْقَبْرِ | We have entered the evening, and the dominion has entered the evening belonging to Allah; all praise is for Allah. None has the right to be worshipped but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. My Lord, I ask You for the good of this night and the good of what follows it, and I seek refuge in You from the evil of this night and the evil of what follows it. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from laziness and the misery of old age. My Lord, I seek refuge in You from punishment in the Fire and punishment in the grave. | Amsayna wa amsal-mulku lillah, walhamdu lillah, la ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamdu wa huwa ala kulli shay'in qadir. Rabbi as'aluka khayra ma fi hadhihil-laylati wa khayra ma ba'daha, wa a'udhu bika min sharri ma fi hadhihil-laylati wa sharri ma ba'daha. Rabbi a'udhu bika minal-kasali wa su'il-kibar. Rabbi a'udhu bika min adhabin fin-nar wa adhabin fil-qabr. | Status: Sahih (Sahih Muslim, Ibn Mas'ud). The Prophet (peace be upon him) used to say this in the evening, and the same words with "asbahna" in the morning.
---1
# By You we reach the evening
أَللَّهُمَّ بِكَ أَمْسَيْنَا وَبِكَ أَصْبَحْنَا وَبِكَ نَحْيَا وَبِكَ نَمُوتُ وَإِلَيْكَ ٱلْمَصِيرُ | O Allah, by You we reach the evening and by You we reach the morning; by You we live and by You we die, and to You is the final return. | Allahumma bika amsayna, wa bika asbahna, wa bika nahya, wa bika namutu, wa ilaykal-masir. | Status: Sahih (Sunan Abi Dawud 5068, graded sahih by al-Albani; at-Tirmidhi 3391: hasan), Abu Hurairah. The ending varies between narrations and editions (an-nushur / al-masir); this follows Hisn al-Muslim.
---1
# Refuge from the evil of the self
أَللَّهُمَّ عَالِمَ ٱلْغَيْبِ وَٱلشَّهَادَةِ فَاطِرَ ٱلسَّمَاوَاتِ وَٱلْأَرْضِ رَبَّ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ وَمَلِيكَهُ أَشْهَدُ أَنْ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنْتَ أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّ نَفْسِى وَمِنْ شَرِّ ٱلشَّيْطَانِ وَشِرْكِهِ وَأَنْ أَقْتَرِفَ عَلَىٰ نَفْسِى سُوٓءًا أَوْ أَجُرَّهُ إِلَىٰ مُسْلِمٍ | O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord and King of everything: I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my own self, from the evil of Satan and the shirk he calls to, and from doing wrong to myself or bringing it upon another Muslim. | Allahumma alimal-ghaybi wash-shahadah, fatiras-samawati wal-ard, rabba kulli shay'in wa malikah, ash-hadu an la ilaha illa anta, a'udhu bika min sharri nafsi wa min sharrish-shaytani wa shirkih, wa an aqtarifa ala nafsi su'an aw ajurrahu ila muslim. | Status: Sahih (Sunan Abi Dawud 5067, al-Albani; at-Tirmidhi: hasan sahih). Abu Bakr asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) for words to say in the morning, in the evening and on going to bed, and he taught him these.
---1
# Pardon, well-being and protection
أَللَّهُمَّ إِنِّىَ أَسْأَلُكَ ٱلْعَفْوَ وَٱلْعَافِيَةَ فِى ٱلدُّنْيَا وَٱلْآخِرَةِ أَللَّهُمَّ إِنِّىَ أَسْأَلُكَ ٱلْعَفْوَ وَٱلْعَافِيَةَ فِى دِينِى وَدُنْيَاىَ وَأَهْلِى وَمَالِى أَللَّهُمَّ ٱسْتُرْ عَوْرَاتِى وَءَامِنْ رَوْعَاتِى أَللَّهُمَّ ٱحْفَظْنِى مِنْ بَيْنِ يَدَىَّ وَمِنْ خَلْفِى وَعَنْ يَمِينِى وَعَنْ شِمَالِى وَمِنْ فَوْقِى وَأَعُوذُ بِعَظَمَتِكَ أَنْ أُغْتَالَ مِنْ تَحْتِى | O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in this world and the next. O Allah, I ask You for pardon and well-being in my religion, my worldly life, my family and my wealth. O Allah, cover my faults and calm my fears. O Allah, protect me from in front of me and from behind me, from my right and from my left, and from above me; and I seek refuge in Your greatness from being struck down from beneath me. | Allahumma inni as'alukal-afwa wal-afiyata fid-dunya wal-akhirah. Allahumma inni as'alukal-afwa wal-afiyata fi dini wa dunyaya wa ahli wa mali. Allahummastur awrati wa amin raw'ati. Allahummahfadhni min bayni yadayya wa min khalfi wa an yamini wa an shimali wa min fawqi, wa a'udhu bi'azamatika an ughtala min tahti. | Status: Sahih (Sunan Abi Dawud 5074, al-Albani). Ibn Umar said the Prophet (peace be upon him) never left these words in the morning or the evening.
---1
# On the fitrah of Islam
أَمْسَيْنَا عَلَىٰ فِطْرَةِ ٱلْإِسْلَامِ وَعَلَىٰ كَلِمَةِ ٱلْإِخْلَاصِ وَعَلَىٰ دِينِ نَبِيِّنَا مُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ وَعَلَىٰ مِلَّةِ أَبِينَا إِبْرَاهِيمَ حَنِيفًا مُسْلِمًا وَمَا كَانَ مِنَ ٱلْمُشْرِكِينَ | We have entered the evening upon the natural way of Islam, upon the word of sincere devotion, upon the religion of our Prophet Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, and upon the way of our father Ibrahim, who was upright, submitting to Allah, and never one of the polytheists. | Amsayna ala fitratil-islam, wa ala kalimatil-ikhlas, wa ala dini nabiyyina Muhammadin sallallahu alayhi wa sallam, wa ala millati abina Ibrahima hanifan musliman wa ma kana minal-mushrikin. | Status: Sahih according to Shu'ayb al-Arna'ut (Ubayy ibn Ka'b, Zawa'id al-Musnad 21144); Ibn Hajar graded the report of Abd ar-Rahman ibn Abza hasan (Musnad Ahmad 15360). The reports give the morning wording; the evening form with "amsayna" follows Hisn al-Muslim.
---3
# Surat al-Ikhlas
بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ | In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. | Bismillahir-rahmanir-rahim | Status: Quran. The count of three, morning and evening, comes from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Khubayb (Abu Dawud, at-Tirmidhi); its grading was not checked for this profile. Reported reward: reciting the three surahs suffices you against everything.
قُلْ هُوَ ٱللَّهُ أَحَدٌ | Say: He is Allah, the One. | Qul huwallahu ahad.
ٱللَّهُ ٱلصَّمَدُ | Allah, the Eternal Refuge. | Allahus-samad.
لَمْ يَلِدْ وَلَمْ يُولَدْ | He has not begotten, nor was He begotten, | Lam yalid wa lam yulad.
وَلَمْ يَكُن لَّهُۥ كُفُوًا أَحَدٌۢ | and there is none equal to Him. | Wa lam yakun lahu kufuwan ahad.
---3
# Surat al-Falaq
بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ | In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. | Bismillahir-rahmanir-rahim | Status: Quran. The count of three, morning and evening, comes from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Khubayb (Abu Dawud, at-Tirmidhi); its grading was not checked for this profile. Reported reward: reciting the three surahs suffices you against everything.
قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ ٱلْفَلَقِ | Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of daybreak, | Qul a'udhu birabbil-falaq,
مِن شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ | from the evil of what He has created, | min sharri ma khalaq,
وَمِن شَرِّ غَاسِقٍ إِذَا وَقَبَ | from the evil of the darkness when it settles, | wa min sharri ghasiqin idha waqab,
وَمِن شَرِّ ٱلنَّفَّٰثَٰتِ فِى ٱلْعُقَدِ | from the evil of those who blow on knots, | wa min sharrin-naffathati fil-uqad,
وَمِن شَرِّ حَاسِدٍ إِذَا حَسَدَ | and from the evil of an envier when he envies. | wa min sharri hasidin idha hasad.
---3
# Surat an-Nas
بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلرَّحْمَٰنِ ٱلرَّحِيمِ | In the name of Allah, the Most Gracious, the Most Merciful. | Bismillahir-rahmanir-rahim | Status: Quran. The count of three, morning and evening, comes from the hadith of Abdullah ibn Khubayb (Abu Dawud, at-Tirmidhi); its grading was not checked for this profile. Reported reward: reciting the three surahs suffices you against everything.
قُلْ أَعُوذُ بِرَبِّ ٱلنَّاسِ | Say: I seek refuge in the Lord of mankind, | Qul a'udhu birabbin-nas,
مَلِكِ ٱلنَّاسِ | the King of mankind, | malikin-nas,
إِلَٰهِ ٱلنَّاسِ | the God of mankind, | ilahin-nas,
مِن شَرِّ ٱلْوَسْوَاسِ ٱلْخَنَّاسِ | from the evil of the whisperer who slinks away, | min sharril-waswasil-khannas,
ٱلَّذِى يُوَسْوِسُ فِى صُدُورِ ٱلنَّاسِ | who whispers in the hearts of mankind, | alladhi yuwaswisu fi sudurin-nas,
مِنَ ٱلْجِنَّةِ وَٱلنَّاسِ | from among jinn and mankind. | minal-jinnati wan-nas.
---3
# Nothing harms with His name
بِسْمِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلَّذِى لَا يَضُرُّ مَعَ ٱسْمِهِ شَىْءٌ فِى ٱلْأَرْضِ وَلَا فِى ٱلسَّمَآءِ وَهُوَ ٱلسَّمِيعُ ٱلْعَلِيمُ | In the name of Allah, with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm; and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing. | Bismillahil-ladhi la yadurru ma'asmihi shay'un fil-ardi wa la fis-sama'i wa huwas-sami'ul-alim. | Status: Sahih (Abu Dawud, at-Tirmidhi 3388: hasan sahih, Ibn Majah, Ahmad; graded sahih by al-Albani), Uthman ibn Affan. Reward: whoever says it three times in the morning will not be struck by a sudden calamity until evening, and whoever says it three times in the evening, not until morning.
---3
# Refuge in Allah’s perfect words
أَعُوذُ بِكَلِمَاتِ ٱللَّهِ ٱلتَّامَّاتِ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا خَلَقَ | I seek refuge in Allah's perfect words from the evil of what He has created. | A'udhu bikalimatillahit-tammati min sharri ma khalaq. | Status: Sahih (at-Tirmidhi 3604: hasan; al-Albani: sahih, Sahih at-Targhib 652), Abu Hurairah. Sahih Muslim 2709 has the same words without the count or the evening timing. Reward: whoever says it three times in the evening, no venomous sting will harm him that night.
---10
# La ilaha illallah, ten times
لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا ٱللَّهُ وَحْدَهُ لَا شَرِيكَ لَهُ لَهُ ٱلْمُلْكُ وَلَهُ ٱلْحَمْدُ وَهُوَ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ شَىْءٍ قَدِيرٌ | There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He has power over all things. | La ilaha illallahu wahdahu la sharika lah, lahul-mulku wa lahul-hamd, wa huwa ala kulli shay'in qadir. | Status: Sahih wording and reward (Sahih al-Bukhari and Sahih Muslim, Abu Ayyub al-Ansari). Timing: the hadith gives none; Hisn al-Muslim lists it among the morning and evening adhkar, and that placement was not verified here. Reward: said ten times, it is like freeing four slaves from the descendants of Isma'il.
---100
# Subhanallahi wa bihamdihi, a hundred times
سُبْحَانَ ٱللَّهِ وَبِحَمْدِهِ | Glory be to Allah, and praise to Him. | Subhanallahi wa bihamdih. | Status: Sahih (Sahih Muslim, Abu Hurairah). Reward: whoever says it a hundred times in the morning and a hundred times in the evening will not be surpassed on the Day of Resurrection by anyone, except one who said the same or more.
---100
# Seeking forgiveness
أَسْتَغْفِرُ ٱللَّهَ وَأَتُوبُ إِلَيْهِ | I ask Allah's forgiveness, and I turn back to Him in repentance. | Astaghfirullaha wa atubu ilayh. | Status: Sahih (Sahih al-Bukhari 6307: more than seventy times a day; Sahih Muslim: a hundred times a day). The Prophet (peace be upon him) said he asked Allah's forgiveness and turned to Him in repentance every day.
---1
# O Ever-Living, O Sustainer
يَا حَىُّ يَا قَيُّومُ بِرَحْمَتِكَ أَسْتَغِيثُ أَصْلِحْ لِى شَأْنِى كُلَّهُ وَلَا تَكِلْنِى إِلَىٰ نَفْسِى طَرْفَةَ عَيْنٍ | O Ever-Living, O Self-Sustaining, I call for help through Your mercy. Set right all my affairs for me, and do not leave me to myself even for the blink of an eye. | Ya Hayyu ya Qayyum, birahmatika astaghith, aslih li sha'ni kullah, wa la takilni ila nafsi tarfata ayn. | Status: Hasan, disputed. al-Albani, Shu'ayb al-Arna'ut and Ibn Hajar graded it hasan, but some of its chains contain weak narrators. The Prophet (peace be upon him) told his daughter Fatimah to say this in the morning and evening. Source: an-Nasa'i (as-Sunan al-Kubra) and al-Hakim, Anas ibn Malik.
---1
# Thanks for every blessing
أَللَّهُمَّ مَآ أَمْسَىٰ بِى مِنْ نِعْمَةٍ أَوْ بِأَحَدٍ مِنْ خَلْقِكَ فَمِنْكَ وَحْدَكَ لَا شَرِيكَ لَكَ فَلَكَ ٱلْحَمْدُ وَلَكَ ٱلشُّكْرُ | O Allah, whatever blessing has come to me this evening, or to any of Your creation, is from You alone with no partner; so to You belongs the praise, and to You the thanks. | Allahumma ma amsa bi min ni'matin aw bi'ahadin min khalqika faminka wahdaka la sharika laka, falakal-hamdu wa lakash-shukr. | Status: Weak chain, no liar found. al-Albani: weak, as the narrator Abdullah ibn Anbasa is barely known. Reward (per the report): whoever says it in the morning has given thanks for that day, and in the evening, for that night. Source: Sunan Abi Dawud 5073, Abdullah ibn Ghannam.
---1
# The good of this night
أَمْسَيْنَا وَأَمْسَى ٱلْمُلْكُ لِلَّهِ رَبِّ ٱلْعَالَمِينَ أَللَّهُمَّ إِنِّى أَسْأَلُكَ خَيْرَ هَٰذِهِ ٱللَّيْلَةِ فَتْحَهَا وَنَصْرَهَا وَنُورَهَا وَبَرَكَتَهَا وَهُدَاهَا وَأَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ شَرِّ مَا فِيهَا وَشَرِّ مَا بَعْدَهَا | We have entered the evening, and the dominion has entered the evening belonging to Allah, Lord of the worlds. O Allah, I ask You for the good of this night: its opening, its victory, its light, its blessing and its guidance; and I seek refuge in You from the evil in it and the evil that comes after it. | Amsayna wa amsal-mulku lillahi rabbil-alamin. Allahumma inni as'aluka khayra hadhihil-laylah: fathaha wa nasraha wa nuraha wa barakataha wa hudaha, wa a'udhu bika min sharri ma fiha wa sharri ma ba'daha. | Status: Weak according to al-Albani; an-Nawawi noted that Abu Dawud did not declare it weak. Source: Sunan Abi Dawud 5084, Abu Malik al-Ash'ari.
---3
# Well-being in body, hearing and sight
أَللَّهُمَّ عَافِنِى فِى بَدَنِى أَللَّهُمَّ عَافِنِى فِى سَمْعِى أَللَّهُمَّ عَافِنِى فِى بَصَرِى لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنْتَ أَللَّهُمَّ إِنِّى أَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنَ ٱلْكُفْرِ وَٱلْفَقْرِ وَأَعُوذُ بِكَ مِنْ عَذَابِ ٱلْقَبْرِ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنْتَ | O Allah, grant me well-being in my body. O Allah, grant me well-being in my hearing. O Allah, grant me well-being in my sight. There is no god but You. O Allah, I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty, and I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave. There is no god but You. | Allahumma afini fi badani, Allahumma afini fi sam'i, Allahumma afini fi basari, la ilaha illa anta. Allahumma inni a'udhu bika minal-kufri wal-faqr, wa a'udhu bika min adhabil-qabr, la ilaha illa anta. | Status: Hasan, disputed. al-Albani: the chain is sahih (Sahih an-Nasa'i 1346); Ibn Hajar: hasan; an-Nasa'i noted that the narrator Ja'far ibn Maymun is not strong. Abu Bakrah said he heard the Prophet (peace be upon him) say these words and loved to follow his Sunnah, repeating them three times morning and evening. Source: Sunan Abi Dawud 5090 and Musnad Ahmad.
---3
# Pleased with Allah as my Lord
رَضِيتُ بِٱللَّهِ رَبًّا وَبِٱلْإِسْلَامِ دِينًا وَبِمُحَمَّدٍ صَلَّى ٱللَّهُ عَلَيْهِ وَسَلَّمَ نَبِيًّا | I am pleased with Allah as my Lord, with Islam as my religion, and with Muhammad, peace and blessings be upon him, as my Prophet. | Raditu billahi rabba, wa bil-islami dina, wa bi-Muhammadin sallallahu alayhi wa sallama nabiyya. | Status: Hasan or sahih through supporting reports. Thawban's chain (at-Tirmidhi 3389) includes Sa'id ibn al-Marzuban, who is weak, and al-Albani weakened it; a parallel report in Musnad Ahmad from a Companion who served the Prophet, with three times morning and evening, was graded sahih li-ghayrihi by Shu'ayb al-Arna'ut. Reward: it is a right upon Allah to please him on the Day of Resurrection.
---4
# Calling Allah to witness
أَللَّهُمَّ إِنِّى أَمْسَيْتُ أُشْهِدُكَ وَأُشْهِدُ حَمَلَةَ عَرْشِكَ وَمَلَآئِكَتَكَ وَجَمِيعَ خَلْقِكَ أَنَّكَ أَنْتَ ٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّآ أَنْتَ وَحْدَكَ لَا شَرِيكَ لَكَ وَأَنَّ مُحَمَّدًا عَبْدُكَ وَرَسُولُكَ | O Allah, this evening I call You to witness, and I call to witness the bearers of Your Throne, Your angels and all Your creation, that You are Allah, there is no god but You alone with no partner, and that Muhammad is Your servant and Your messenger. | Allahumma inni amsaytu ushhiduka, wa ushhidu hamalata arshika wa mala'ikataka wa jami'a khalqika, annaka antallahu la ilaha illa anta wahdaka la sharika laka, wa anna Muhammadan abduka wa rasuluk. | Status: Weak chain, no liar found. Sunan Abi Dawud 5069, Anas ibn Malik: the chain has an unknown narrator and a disputed link from Makhul to Anas. al-Albani: weak; Ibn Baz: hasan. Reward (per the report): whoever says it four times in the morning or evening, Allah frees him from the Fire.
---7
# Allah is enough for me
حَسْبِىَ ٱللَّهُ لَآ إِلَٰهَ إِلَّا هُوَ عَلَيْهِ تَوَكَّلْتُ وَهُوَ رَبُّ ٱلْعَرْشِ ٱلْعَظِيمِ | Allah is enough for me; there is no god but Him. In Him I place my trust, and He is the Lord of the Mighty Throne. | Hasbiyallahu la ilaha illa huwa, alayhi tawakkaltu wa huwa rabbul-arshil-azim. | Status: Disputed; keep or remove as you judge. The words are Quran (9:129). The count of seven, morning and evening, and the reward come from Sunan Abi Dawud 5081, a report from Abu ad-Darda'. Shu'ayb al-Arna'ut: its narrators are trustworthy but it has an added phrase he rejects; Ibn Baz: good chain; al-Albani: fabricated. Reward (per the report): Allah suffices him in whatever concerns him of this world and the next.
---10
# Blessings on the Prophet
أَللَّهُمَّ صَلِّ وَسَلِّمْ عَلَىٰ نَبِيِّنَا مُحَمَّدٍ | O Allah, send prayers and peace upon our Prophet Muhammad. | Allahumma salli wa sallim ala nabiyyina Muhammad. | Status: Weak (broken chain). Reported by at-Tabarani from Abu ad-Darda'; Khalid ibn Ma'dan did not hear from him. al-Albani first graded it hasan, then weak; Ibn Baz: not known to be authentic. Whether the full chain has a liar was not checked. Sending blessings on the Prophet is commanded in the Quran (33:56); only the count of ten, morning and evening, and the reward rest on this report. Reward (per the report): his intercession on the Day of Resurrection.
